# Veil agent workflow (knowledge layer)

Follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md), [docs/agents/coding-style.md](../../docs/agents/coding-style.md), [core-karpathy-guidelines.mdc](core-karpathy-guidelines.mdc), and [core-kaizen.mdc](core-kaizen.mdc).

**Pentest execution:** [veneno](https://github.com/butbeautifulv/veneno) — not in this repo.

## Architecture (do not break)

- Three contexts: `discovery/`, `pipeline/`, `knowledge/` — **no cross-layer Go imports**.
- TI integration via NATS (`scrape.>` → `ingest.>`).
- Engage ingest bridge: `pipeline/engage-events` consumes `engage.events.*` from veneno.
- No root `go.work`.

## Multi-phase work

1. Master plan → phase plan → branch → implement → critic → merge → docs ([core-workflow-chain.mdc](core-workflow-chain.mdc)).

## Required before finishing

1. `make test-discovery`, `make test-pipeline`, `make test-knowledge` for touched layers.
2. Graph version bump if ingest paths changed (`make check-graph-version`).
3. Commit, push, update docs per [core-agent-documentation.mdc](core-agent-documentation.mdc).

## Git hygiene

- Never commit `data/`, secrets, or `**/__pycache__/`.
